+/*
+ * Client of the isolated BD-J host (bdr_protocol.h), in the player's process.
+ *
+ * Threads, all ended by bdr_client_close():
+ *  - the caller: a forwarded call sends BDR_CALL and waits for its BDR_REPLY. HDMV overlays that
+ *    the host drew during that call are delivered by the caller, in order, before the call
+ *    returns, as libbluray does when it plays locally (the callback then runs inside the call).
+ *  - the receiver reads every message. It never calls the player and never waits for it: it
+ *    hands replies to their caller, file requests to the file thread and overlays to the
+ *    callback thread; it copies the pixels of an ARGB update out of the shared memory and
+ *    acknowledges them at once.
+ *  - the file thread serves the host's file and directory requests from the player's disc.
+ *  - the callback thread delivers the ARGB updates and the HDMV overlays drawn outside a call.
+ * So a player callback that blocks can never hold up the disc reads the host waits for: the
+ * callbacks are where libbluray calls them when it plays locally, and nothing more depends on
+ * them returning.
+ */
+
